{"_meta":{"lovie/risk":"read","openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Loaded","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Loading\u2026","openai/visibility":"public","securitySchemes":[{"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Proposes a native Mac secure action sheet or confirmation card. It refuses with 'This chat cannot show secure cards' when the chat the member is using cannot show them; then continue in plain text or with the app handoff in the same turn. Pass only the exact action kind and IDs from record reads. No secret, visa number, tax identifier, transfer code, approval session ID, or arbitrary arguments are accepted. This does not execute anything. The founder enters private data and approves in the native app; read the record again before claiming success. Company ID is required for every action: a proposal without one is refused, so a formation with no company yet continues through the secure formation app handoff. Domain actions take company_id and domain; application and MONEY_RECEIVE actions take resource_id; SIGNATURE_SEND takes resource_ref (the env_ envelope id) and no resource_id; child tax actions also take subject_id. Transfers still draft, get phone approval and commit through the transfer tools. When the source account and/or the recipient is ambiguous, TRANSFER_SEND may be proposed with company_id and transfer (amount_cents, rail, optional memo, the one known source_account_id or recipient_id, optional recipient_query) so the founder picks the rest; it moves no money, and the chosen ids must be checked against list_accounts and list_send_recipients before drafting. Never call raw sensitive setters or request a value in chat.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"action":{"properties":{"companyId":{"description":"UUID value wrapper.","properties":{"value":{"format":"uuid","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"domain":{"maxLength":253,"pattern":"^$|^[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]*[a-z0-9])?(\\.[a-z0-9]([a